  "plain": "The film director Steven Spielberg is said to have binge-watched all 72 episodes of The Secret of Skinwalker Ranch, a TV series about a Utah property famous for strange sightings, before making his film Disclosure Day, pointing to the congressional hearings and the government's growing acknowledgement that the phenomenon is real. Brandon Fugal, the businessman who owns the ranch, relays this as Spielberg told it, which suggests that one of the world's best-known filmmakers took the show seriously."
